  "properties": {
    "title": "How many coordinate systems are in a web map?",
    "description": "A default web map takes data in latitude-longitude and displays it in spherical Mercator, which makes two different coordinate systems. But the internal workings of a mapping library require handling even more coordinate systems internally.\r\n\r\nThis talk is a deep technical view into how some web map libraries (Leaflet, MapLibre, OpenLayers, Gleo) handle coordinate systems internally, and how their different strategies affect performance in specific scenarios.",
